---
/*
 * Getting started (docs/shep-design/README.md, "Screens > 2. Docs >
 * Getting started"). Copy and command output checked against README.md,
 * the source of truth for anything that could drift (build steps, the
 * Flockfile shape, shep ls output, the JSON envelope).
 *
 * Restructured 2026-09-14 per docs/writing-plans/plans/2026-09-14-docs-part-one.md,
 * Task 3: the five numbered steps are gone. A short version carries the
 * happy path above the fold; everything else moved below it.
 */
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import ReferencePills from "../../components/docs/ReferencePills.astro";
import Callout from "../../components/docs/Callout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/docs/CodeBlock.astro";
import ShortVersion from "../../components/docs/ShortVersion.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  activeSlug="getting-started"
>
  <article>
    <h1>Quickstart</h1>
    <ReferencePills slug="getting-started" />
    <p class="lede">
      Installing shep and getting a flock running takes about two minutes.
    </p>
    <p class="fine">
      Already running pm2? Start at{" "}
      <a href="/docs/from-pm2">Coming from pm2</a> instead.
    </p>

    <ShortVersion>
      <div class="terminal">
        <div><span class="prompt">$</span> cargo install shep</div>
      </div>
      <div class="file-panel">
        <div class="file-name">Flockfile.toml</div>
        <div class="file-body">
          <div class="bark-line">[[app]]</div>
          <div>name&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;= <span class="str">"web"</span></div>
          <div>script = <span class="str">"./server"</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="terminal">
        <div><span class="prompt">$</span> shep start Flockfile.toml</div>
        <div><span class="prompt">$</span> shep ls</div>
      </div>
    </ShortVersion>
    <p class="fine">
      <code>./server</code> is your own binary or start script, and shep
      writes neither: point <code>script</code> at something that already
      exists or the start fails to spawn. Nothing to hand yet?{" "}
      <code>shep serve ./site</code> puts a real sheep in the flock out of
      the install you just did, no Flockfile needed. See{" "}
      <a href="/docs/serve">Serve</a>.
    </p>

    <Callout variant="careful">
      shep is pre-1.0, so anything here can still change. macOS, Linux and
      Windows all work; the Windows tier is newer, and two limits are worth
      knowing before you rely on it: <code>shep stop</code> has no graceful
      signal to send unless your app reads the shepherd channel, and{" "}
      <code>shep startup</code> is not built there. Your flock lives in{" "}
      <code>%USERPROFILE%\.shep</code> on Windows, since it sets no{" "}
      <code>HOME</code>.
    </Callout>

    <h2 id="other-installs">Other ways to install</h2>
    <p>Homebrew:</p>
    <div class="terminal">
      <div><span class="prompt">$</span> brew install shep-pm/shep/shep</div>
    </div>
    <p>Scoop:</p>
    <div class="terminal">
      <div><span class="prompt">&gt;</span> scoop bucket add shep https://github.com/shep-pm/scoop-shep</div>
      <div><span class="prompt">&gt;</span> scoop install shep</div>
    </div>
    <p class="fine">
      If <code>shep.exe</code> will not start, it wants the Visual C++
      redistributable: <code>scoop bucket add extras</code>, then
      <code>scoop install extras/vcredist2022</code>.
    </p>
    <p>Prebuilt binaries:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/shep-pm/shep/releases/latest/download/shep-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz">macOS, Apple silicon</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/shep-pm/shep/releases/latest/download/shep-x86_64-apple-darwin.tar.gz">macOS, Intel</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/shep-pm/shep/releases/latest/download/shep-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz">Linux x86-64</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/shep-pm/shep/releases/latest/download/shep-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz">Linux x86-64, static</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/shep-pm/shep/releases/latest/download/shep-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz">Linux arm64</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/shep-pm/shep/releases/latest/download/shep-aarch64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz">Linux arm64, static</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/shep-pm/shep/releases/latest/download/shep-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip">Windows x86-64</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="fine">
      Each link redirects to the newest release. Checksums are in{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/shep-pm/shep/releases/latest/download/SHA256SUMS">SHA256SUMS</a>.
    </p>
    <p>Or build it yourself:</p>
    <div class="terminal">
      <div><span class="prompt">$</span> git clone https://github.com/shep-pm/shep.git</div>
      <div><span class="prompt">$</span> cd shep</div>
      <div><span class="prompt">$</span> cargo build --release</div>
      <div><span class="prompt">$</span> ./target/release/shep --help</div>
    </div>
    <p class="fine">
      Rust 1.88 or newer, edition 2024.
    </p>
    <details id="completions-and-welcome">
      <summary>Shell completions and the first-run greeting</summary>
      <p>
        <code>shep completions &lt;shell&gt;</code> prints a completion
        script for your shell. It completes verbs and flags only, never
        sheep or fold names.{" "}
        <code>shep welcome</code> reprints the one-time greeting a fresh{" "}
        <code>$SHEP_HOME</code> shows on its own.
      </p>
    </details>

    <h2 id="interpreters">Scripts that need an interpreter</h2>
    <p>
      <code>script</code> is run directly, so a compiled binary or a file
      with a shebang and the executable bit needs nothing further. A plain{" "}
      <code>server.js</code> has neither, and shep will not guess: guessing
      is how a process manager ends up with opinions you did not ask for.
    </p>
    <p>
      Instead you tell it once. On first run shep writes a starter mapping
      into <code>~/.shep/shep.toml</code>, commented so you can see exactly
      what it will do:
    </p>
    <CodeBlock label="~/.shep/shep.toml">{`[interpreters]
js = "node"
py = "python3"
sh = "sh"`}</CodeBlock>
    <p>
      From then on <code>shep start server.js</code> works. The table is
      yours to edit: add an extension, or delete it to turn interpreters
      off. An individual app can override it with its own{" "}
      <code>interpreter</code> field, and a single run can override both
      with <code>--interpreter</code>; the last one named wins.
    </p>

    <h2 id="the-flock-table">Reading the flock table</h2>
    <div class="terminal">
      <div><span class="prompt">$</span> shep ls</div>
      <div class="muted">ID  NAME    STATUS  PID   RESTARTS  EXIT  CFG  CPU    MEM    UPTIME  FOLD     SMIT</div>
      <div>1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;web&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="ok">online</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;1001&nbsp;&nbsp;1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="muted">-</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="muted">-</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;12.5%&nbsp;&nbsp;48.1M&nbsp;&nbsp;1m&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;backend&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="muted">-</span></div>
      <div>2&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;cron&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="ok">online</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;1003&nbsp;&nbsp;3&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="muted">-</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="muted">-</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="muted">-</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;48.1M&nbsp;&nbsp;30s&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;backend&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="muted">-</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="fine">
      The CPU column prints <code>-</code> rather than <code>0.0%</code>{" "}
      when a reading is unavailable, because a confident zero is worse
      than an obvious blank. <code>EXIT</code> uses the same convention,
      and shows why a stopped sheep stopped. <code>CFG</code> reads{" "}
      <code>-</code> until a sheep has config waiting on it; see{" "}
      <a href="/docs/overrides">Overrides</a>.
    </p>
    <div class="alias-grid">
      <div class="alias-card">
        <div class="themed">shep bleats</div>
        <div class="plain">same as shep logs</div>
      </div>
      <div class="alias-card">
        <div class="themed">shep flock</div>
        <div class="plain">same as shep list / ls</div>
      </div>
      <div class="alias-card">
        <div class="themed">shep muster</div>
        <div class="plain">same as resurrect</div>
      </div>
      <div class="alias-card">
        <div class="themed">shep thatlldo</div>
        <div class="plain">same as graceful stop</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 id="json">Piping it somewhere</h2>
    <p>
      Every command renders as <code>--format json</code> too, under a
      versioned envelope, so nothing has to scrape columns.
    </p>
    <div class="terminal json">{"\n"}  <span class="key">"schema_version"</span>: <span class="num">1</span>,{"\n"}  <span class="key">"command"</span>: <span class="s">"flock"</span>,{"\n"}  <span class="key">"data"</span>: [{"\n"}    {"{ "}<span class="key">"id"</span>: <span class="num">1</span>, <span class="key">"name"</span>: <span class="s">"web"</span>, <span class="key">"status"</span>: <span class="s">"online"</span>, <span class="key">"pid"</span>: <span class="num">1001</span>,{"\n"}      <span class="key">"restarts"</span>: <span class="num">1</span>, <span class="key">"uptime_ms"</span>: <span class="num">60000</span>, <span class="key">"fold"</span>: <span class="s">"backend"</span>,{"\n"}      <span class="key">"cpu_percent"</span>: <span class="num">12.5</span>, <span class="key">"memory_bytes"</span>: <span class="num">50462720</span>, <span class="key">"dog"</span>: <span class="nul">null</span> {"}"}{"\n"}  ]{"\n"}{"}"}</div>
</article>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .terminal {
    background: var(--illus-terminal-bg);
    border: 3px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 20px 22px;
    font-family: "Space Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 13.5px;
    line-height: 1.9;
    color: var(--illus-terminal-text);
    overflow-x: auto;
    white-space: pre;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }

  .terminal.json {
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.85;
    margin: 0 0 40px;
  }

  .terminal .prompt,
  .terminal .ok {
    color: var(--grass);
  }

  .terminal .muted {
    color: var(--illus-terminal-muted);
  }

  .terminal .key {
    color: var(--sky);
  }

  .terminal .num,
  .terminal .s {
    color: var(--grass);
  }

  .terminal .nul {
    color: var(--bark);
  }

  .file-panel {
    background: var(--paper-2);
    border: 3px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 16px;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin: 0 0 18px;
  }

  .file-name {
    padding: 12px 18px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--hair);
    font-family: "Space Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .file-body {
    padding: 20px 22px;
    font-family: "Space Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 13.5px;
    line-height: 1.9;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .file-body .bark-line {
    color: var(--bark);
  }

  .file-body .str {
    color: var(--meadow);
  }

  .alias-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(230px, 1fr));
    gap: 14px;
    margin: 0 0 40px;
  }

  .alias-card {
    background: var(--paper-2);
    border: 2.5px solid var(--hair);
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 14px 16px;
  }

  .alias-card .themed {
    font-family: "Space Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--meadow);
  }

  .alias-card .plain {
    font-family: "Space Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    margin-top: 5px;
  }

</style>
